    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (77.62) anchoring the lineup, benefiting from a soft matchup against Cecconi and an elite xwOBA of 0.448 that makes him our primary offensive engine. **Christian Yelich** (74.32) follows close behind; he is arguably our strongest play today due to his optimal leadoff position and a favorable matchup against Elder. Crucially, **Yelich** faces a pitcher with a slow delivery, and given our focus on the scarcity of SB, his potential for base-stealing in this environment significantly inflates his value. **Trea Turner** (68.44) and **Kyle Schwarber** (67.41) remain high-floor options despite the threat of Peterson, as both benefit from favorable projected order placements and a platoon advantage that keeps their efficiency scores comfortably in the elite-adjacent range.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical hurdles today, specifically regarding **Carson Benge**, whose score dropped to 45.89 due to a challenging matchup against the formidable Zack Wheeler. While **Benge** retains utility as a leadoff hitter, the SP skill penalty is substantial. On the bench, **Caleb Durbin** was the primary consideration for a spot, but his 41.23 efficiency score was hampered by a difficult matchup against Gilbert. We opted to prioritize the platoon advantages of **Casey Schmitt** (62.41) and **Lars Nootbaar** (64.36) instead, as both are slated for higher-leverage opportunities against favorable opposing arms. Note that **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is unavailable due to a rainout, and we continue to monitor **Hyeseong Kim** and **Rece Hinds** in the minors, ensuring our active roster remains focused on the 5x5 categories that currently drive our competitive standing.",
